<title>BELGIUM: EU cereals panel allows extra 1,300 T millet quota.</title>
<headline>EU cereals panel allows extra 1,300 T millet quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee has voted to allow an additional import quota of 1,300 tonnes of millet, an EU official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The additonal quota required under the Article 24/6 GATT (General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade) arrangement covering Austria's entry to the EU was approved,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The quota will be subject to a reduced import tariff of seven Ecus per tonne, the official said.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
